M2 Ultra + DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 EXL3 EAQ v1 2.9 bpw
Maintained by chenwenhao0326-arch.

This is an independent deployment and engineering adaptation. It is not an
official DeepSeek, Apple, mlx-serve, mlx-stream, Sushi or Mia-AiLab release.

Core engine:
  mlx-serve — David Dalcu and contributors
  https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
  Pinned 94670d961c5b6934dc8d91c7b8be68bf44b60981.
  MIT plus upstream third-party notices, reproduced under licenses/.
  Local changes include plugin host seams, text/agent protocol compatibility,
  request shaping, and frontend stream timeout handling.

Streaming plugin:
  mlx-stream — David Tai and contributors
  https://github.com/davidtai/mlx-stream
  Pinned fcb4011347ff80eeeb19e2a1f0180e13199c7c8b.
  MIT; its complete NOTICE is reproduced under licenses/.
  Local changes include native state/prefix reuse, prefill/cache scheduling,
  measured M2 kernel integration and selective extension-cache retention.

Method and implementation references:
  Sushi — https://github.com/beamivalice/sushi (MIT)
  M2 SIMD adaptation references 3f3ff7bcf4775ae2e88a8e9c36d2715fcfd9f7cf.
  Selective cache-release planning references b68302a1469ed7d2dab03530cc10c6e2685f2a0a,
  src/dsv41_borrow.zig, Engine.borrowLayer and Engine.restoreLayer.
  The local EXL3 implementation releases inactive extension owners, retaining
  the base pool and original native memory bill. It does not copy STQ weights
  or claim the author's M5/STQ performance on M2/EXL3.
  M2 decode grouping also references Strata's load-reuse methodology; exact
  inherited attributions and license texts are in licenses/m2-adapter-NOTICE.txt.

Generated Metal/C adapter:
  Includes code derived from Apple MLX, mlx-stream, Sushi and other sources
  enumerated in licenses/m2-adapter-NOTICE.txt and mlx-serve-NOTICE.txt.
  MIT and applicable Apache-2.0 notices are retained in licenses/.

Model provenance (weights are obtained separately):
  DeepSeek-AI: DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 original model.
  Mia-AiLab: EXL3 EAQ v1 2.9-bpw quantization, using ExLlamaV3 by turboderp.
  OpensourceWTF: streaming repack consumed by this runtime.
  Exact repositories and revisions are recorded in sources.lock.json.
  We did not train, quantize or author these model weights.

Local engineering and packaging were developed with AI coding assistance.
